<div class="mw-parser-output"><h1>Comm</h1>
<p>Channels let you talk with players all over the world. Anyone can start a 
channel: just add one with a name nobody uses, and tell your friends to add 
it too. Your channels are saved with your character.
</p><p>Usage:
</p>
<pre>comm add &lt;channel&gt;        start or join a channel
comm delete &lt;channel&gt;     leave a channel
<a cmd='#'>comm #</a>                  list the channels you are on
&lt;channel&gt; &lt;message&gt;       talk on a channel
&lt;channel&gt; @ &lt;action&gt;      an emote on a channel
&lt;channel&gt; #               see who is on a channel
comm inform on|off|join   see who joins and leaves your channels
<a cmd='#'>comm echo</a>               turn on or off seeing your own messages
<a cmd='#'>comm help</a>               a short list of these commands
</pre>
<p>For example, to join the newbie channel and ask a question:
</p>
<pre>comm add newbie
newbie How do I get my corpse back?
</pre>
<p>Some channels are relayed to the game's Discord server, and what you write on 
them is public there too: newbie, chat, mud, bugs, builder, accessibility and 
diku3. <a cmd='#'>comm #</a> shows which of these you are on. The guild channel, gchat, 
only reaches members of your own guild.
</p><p>Keep the public channels friendly: no swearing, and no advertising other games 
or web pages. Offenders lose the use of their channels for a while.
</p><p><br />
See Also:
</p>
<pre>&gt; <a cmd='#'>Help Shout</a>
&gt; <a cmd='#'>Help Say</a>
&gt; <a cmd='#'>Help Tell</a>
&gt; <a cmd='#'>Help Newbie</a>
</pre>




</div>